# Ruling (CR 707.10): a copy of a bargained spell is also bargained. Bot1 has Leyline of Resonance out and casts Torch the Tower
# bargained, sacrificing Shared Animosity (an enchantment), at its own Ornithopter; the Leyline copies the spell and the copy is
# aimed at Bot2's Keen-Eyed Curator (a 3/3). The copy deals 3, not 2, and the Curator is exiled instead of dying, and the copy
# scries 1 as well as the original (two scries asked). The original then kills the Ornithopter, exiled too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Leyline of Resonance
Black Lotus
Shared Animosity
Mox Ruby
Torch the Tower
Ornithopter
Mountain
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Forest
Keen-Eyed Curator
Forest x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Shared Animosity.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Keen-Eyed Curator.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Torch the Tower.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Modes(Bargain:)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Shared Animosity)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Keen-Eyed Curator)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Mountain | )
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Mountain | )
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Keen-Eyed Curator; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Stack.Count = 0
